        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Ah, I think I see. The registry is user-accessible so users can add pickers to it, but it's really only meant to be _used_ by the Pick command. I was using pickers through the registry in my own config (because I had just learned about it; new thing to try 🙂), but I should have just been accessing the pickers directly.\n\nYes, exactly. The built-in pickers are there in their own places (`MiniPick.builtin` and `MiniExtra.pickers`) and can/should be called from them if used in Lua code.\n`MiniPick.registry` is more for users/plugins to add their own pickers to be used through `:Pick`. To use them from Lua code, those can be accessed directly from their original place (user config or plugin source).",
